<!-- ReferralSeam — the invitee half of "Invite friends" (docs/design/reference-ui-spec.md
     §9.3 row 5), a 0×0 mount with one job: if this install landed through an invite link
     (Components/Invite.dsx wrote the code into the `sd_ref` cookie), attach it to the
     device's identity the moment there is one. Mounted on Home and on Rewards, so a cold
     link lands the attachment on the first screen a viewer sees.

     THE COOKIE IS SPENT ONCE, WHATEVER THE ANSWER: a code the server refuses (unknown, the
     viewer's own, or a device that has already watched) is not worth a retry loop, and a
     stale cookie retrying on every mount would be a request the rate ceiling eventually
     refuses for a real reason. The grant is never this device's: the inviter is credited
     when THIS device records its first server-verified minute (server/engage.dsx watchTick
     writes the proof; claimTask sweeps it). -->
<stack width="0" height="0" on:appear="dsx.action.attachIfAny()">
  <head>
    <api as="attach" url="/rewards/referral" method="POST" auto="false" headers="global.auth.headers"/>
    <variable as="busy">return false</variable>

    <action as="attachIfAny">
      const code = dsx.cookie.sd_ref
      if (code == null) { return }
      if (code == '') { return }
      if (global.auth == null) { return }
      if (global.auth.ok != true) { return }
      if (dsx.variable.busy) { return }
      dsx.variable.busy = true
      const r = await attach.send({ code: code })
      dsx.cookie.sd_ref = ''
      dsx.variable.busy = false
      // the inviter row in /rewards/state reads the proof later; nothing to refresh here
      if (r.ok) { return }
    </action>

    <!-- the seam resolves identity after this mounts on a cold load, so the write waits on it -->
    <watch value="global.auth.ok" on:change="dsx.action.attachIfAny()"/>
  </head>
</stack>
